            <ArticleTitle>Fatal neonatal stroke from a prenatal cardiac thrombus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>140-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pediatrneurol.2007.10.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite careful investigation, the etiology of many perinatal arterial strokes is unknown. We report on a 5-day-old boy with a cardiac thrombus of prenatal origin resulting in a fatal postnatal stroke. The thrombus was discovered only at autopsy, challenging the assumption of a placental source of embolus in perinatal strokes in the absence of macroscopic and microscopic examination of the heart.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
